<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

''HOLD.'' The fixed broker root closes the specific round-7 placement examples, but authority placement remains unsafe across the staging and lane-identity surfaces. Both findings are ''LEAD'' conclusions from source and test inspection, not reproductions.

# ''P1 — The worktree staging root can overlap a granted writable root.'' [[commit-relay.mjs:37|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/commit-relay.mjs:37]] places staging under `.lares-scratch/.broker-worktrees/<lane>` and creates it without checking its components or comparing it with granted roots. [[launch-codex.mjs:370|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/launch-codex.mjs:370]] permits a lead or build worktree anywhere below scratch, including an ancestor of that staging directory; a lead lane can also overlap it. A seat with such a grant can change staging pathnames while [[addWorktree|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/seat-broker.mjs:453]] uses them with broker authority for Git, export, and cleanup. This repeats the ''cross-lane authority-placement and pathname-write class'', across the staging surface. The [[fixed-root test|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/commit-relay.test.mjs:497]] covers the go and iso root, while the [[granted-root test|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/launch-codex.test.mjs:1134]] covers overlap with the fixed root; neither establishes staging isolation.

# ''P1 — Distinct lanes with the same basename share go and broker state.'' [[broker-root.mjs:62|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/broker-root.mjs:62]] derives the lane identity solely from `basename`. Two accepted lane roots with the same basename consequently share both `go/<lane>/push-go` and `iso/<lane>`. A go intended for one can be consumed by the other when branch and head match, including when their controller-configured push targets differ; the relays also share `made.json` and temporary broker state ([[commit-relay.mjs:80|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/commit-relay.mjs:80]]). The [[controller-go test|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/commit-relay.test.mjs:534]] exercises one lane, not colliding lane identities. Bind authority and state to an unambiguous lane identity and include the push destination in the authorization.

These are present broker boundaries, so I would resolve them in this lane rather than defer them to the live-wiki design in row 7.

On the requested confirmations:

* The broker’s [[poison, hook, filter, submodule, and read-race tests|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/commit-relay.test.mjs:186]] support the paths they exercise. Finding 1 prevents confirming the universal no-authority-leak and lane-root claims. The relay rejects lead launches, but finding 2 limits push authorization.
* Marker matching and fail-closed watch tests support ordinary rollout association and stop behavior, including overlapping launches ([[launch-codex.test.mjs:409|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/launch-codex.test.mjs:409]]). I cannot say the watchdog can ''never'' signal the wrong process: the hand-off explicitly accepts the host PID-reuse edge.
* The receipt binds the tree, check names, and definitions; the key and receipts remain in memory. The [[forgery|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/commit-relay.test.mjs:391]] and [[read-only tree|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/commit-relay.test.mjs:403]] tests support those properties, subject to the documented host ptrace and seat seccomp assumptions.
* Missing bubblewrap returns named refusals before check or install code runs, as pinned by the [[refusal test|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/commit-relay.test.mjs:435]]. The [[mode and floor tests|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/launch-codex.test.mjs:365]] cover the stated floors and thresholds; I found no additional floor regression.
* The revised supervisor has targeted tests for [[exceptional completion, live-group retention, and the per-tick size ceiling|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/launch-codex.test.mjs:1153]]. The size ceiling is a sampled stop threshold, not a hard filesystem quota.

I did not run tests, construct payloads, or write files. Green CI at `6fcd541a0`, including live bubblewrap proofs, is a ''MEASURED report supplied in the hand-off'', not an independent measurement by this review.

